WEBVTT

00:00:01.650 --> 00:00:02.520
To the rhythm!

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:05.850
Check it!

00:00:09.430 --> 00:00:10.790
OK, fellas!

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:29.910
Yeah yeah party people
let's go let's turn it up

00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:33.790
Let's rush in let's send it flying
let's attack let's dash

00:00:33.790 --> 00:00:37.460
The battlefields are sacred,
Bakuretsu Tenshi, Crazy Burst Angel

00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:41.260
They're a bother, they're cheeky,
come on, blast 'em good!

00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:46.530
Everybody, loosey

00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:50.230
Be in full bloom, bluesy

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:53.570
Vividly, crazy

00:00:53.570 --> 00:00:56.070
Fly up, angel

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:58.380
We are the risma so charisma

00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:00.480
We soar, really prisma (bomber)

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:02.950
Hey! It's danceable OK
shake it right now let's go

00:01:02.950 --> 00:01:05.750
Gutsiness let's go beat
let's ride the rhythm tension

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:07.390
It goes flying frustration

00:01:07.390 --> 00:01:11.490
Alright let's go let's get it on
loosey beauty get your body

00:01:11.490 --> 00:01:14.990
Everybody, loosey

00:01:14.990 --> 00:01:18.500
Be in full bloom, bluesy

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:21.900
Vividly, crazy

00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:25.270
Fly up, angel

00:01:30.210 --> 00:01:36.480
Besides the 5 km. radius, 2-story
underground, 8-above ground dome,

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:40.380
we plan to build all types of amusement
facilities on this artificial island.

00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:41.650
What is that?

00:01:41.650 --> 00:01:45.190
A 'red tide'. Dead plankton, basically.

00:01:45.190 --> 00:01:50.700
It's a byproduct of our work here;
it's nothing to worry about.

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:53.560
Of course I have nothing to worry about!

00:01:53.560 --> 00:01:55.030
Huh?

00:01:55.030 --> 00:01:59.040
Should anything happen,
<i>you'll</i> be held responsible!

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:03.030
If you don't want to lose your jobs,
then figure out a solution at once!

00:02:13.790 --> 00:02:21.330
The ocean is crying...
The sky is crying...

00:02:21.330 --> 00:02:24.530
--Our future is crying...
--Ridiculous...

00:02:24.530 --> 00:02:28.590
What's the point in worrying
about a future where you don't exist?

00:02:31.270 --> 00:02:35.440
It's been years since I took over
this work from the last governor.

00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:37.510
After overcoming all sorts of problems,

00:02:37.510 --> 00:02:42.550
Tokyo Treasure Island
has finally been completed!

00:02:42.550 --> 00:02:46.980
At long last, the doors to
the dream paradise will open!

00:02:48.690 --> 00:02:51.790
Five, four, three...

00:02:51.790 --> 00:02:53.720
Two, one...

00:03:14.510 --> 00:03:17.750
What a magnificent place!

00:03:17.750 --> 00:03:20.380
--Don't you think, Kyohei-<i>kun</i>?!
--Y-Yeah...

00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:25.420
--What's the deal? You're young!
--I'm not really--

00:03:25.420 --> 00:03:27.260
Check it out!

00:03:27.260 --> 00:03:30.350
--It's perfect!
--Sure is!

00:03:31.930 --> 00:03:35.500
Oh, are you two already
having a good time?

00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:39.240
--Men sure get along well...
--S-Sei-<i>san</i>...!

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:41.540
I'm glad you came along, Jinno-<i>san</i>...

00:03:41.540 --> 00:03:45.840
I'm glad to have such a nice vacation!

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:47.780
By the way, Sei-<i>san</i>...

00:03:47.780 --> 00:03:52.320
How about we enjoy ourselves
as adults once in a while?

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:54.790
Yes. That would be wonderful.

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:57.720
Leo! Above you!

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:01.390
Meg!

00:04:01.390 --> 00:04:04.990
I told him to look out!

00:04:07.130 --> 00:04:11.270
Leo-<i>chan</i>! Come on! Wanna get revenge?

00:04:11.270 --> 00:04:12.840
I'll show you...!

00:04:12.840 --> 00:04:15.640
As males, we can't back down!
Let's go, Kyohei-<i>kun</i>!

00:04:15.640 --> 00:04:18.110
Y-Yeah...

00:04:18.110 --> 00:04:19.840
Have a taste of my fastball!

00:04:19.840 --> 00:04:23.810
Which one are you hitting to?!
You're so dumb!

00:04:23.810 --> 00:04:26.080
You're not going to play?

00:04:26.080 --> 00:04:29.250
Alright! Right here! Right here!

00:04:29.250 --> 00:04:30.080
I'll pass.

00:04:31.690 --> 00:04:35.630
--How are things?
--Working perfectly.

00:04:35.630 --> 00:04:37.700
The big shots keep blabbing about

00:04:37.700 --> 00:04:41.200
the state-of-the-art game machines
and automated restaurants,

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:46.140
but the Super-EM plant that
uses seawater is the real masterpiece!

00:04:46.140 --> 00:04:50.150
Definitely. I'd love to
show this place to people

00:04:50.150 --> 00:04:53.210
who make a fuss about
fake sea-bathing resorts.

00:04:54.720 --> 00:04:56.880
The sky is so high up!

00:04:58.220 --> 00:04:59.650
What're you doing?

00:04:59.650 --> 00:05:02.760
Searching for insider info
on this place.

00:05:02.760 --> 00:05:07.000
You shouldn't spend all your time
on the computer out here!

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:11.900
That's narrow-minded. This happens
to be my favorite thing to do!

00:05:11.900 --> 00:05:13.330
Sure, whatever...

00:05:13.330 --> 00:05:17.370
Anyway, isn't that swimsuit super lame?

00:05:17.370 --> 00:05:20.080
Eh? Do you think so?

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:23.680
--It's not cute at all.
--I see...

00:05:23.680 --> 00:05:29.120
That's not true! It's a great design!

00:05:29.120 --> 00:05:29.950
Right?!

00:05:29.950 --> 00:05:35.320
Yeah, I agree! Do you happen
to be a model or something?

00:05:35.320 --> 00:05:40.460
Say, I think I've seen you
somewhere before. Are you an actress?

00:05:40.460 --> 00:05:44.370
Trying to flatter me?
But I'm happy to hear it!

00:05:44.370 --> 00:05:47.540
You mean you're not?
That's hard to believe...

00:05:47.540 --> 00:05:53.110
But you must be someone special
if you were invited here today...!

00:05:53.110 --> 00:05:55.980
Ugh! What's with you guys?!

00:05:55.980 --> 00:06:00.320
She your kid sister?
Her swimsuit looks cute too!

00:06:00.320 --> 00:06:04.290
Are you in grade school?
Want me to look over your homework?

00:06:04.290 --> 00:06:05.650
<i>Moron...</i>

00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:09.720
Oh? What happened, Jo?

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:13.160
He overdid it a bit and fainted.

00:06:15.660 --> 00:06:19.230
--What happened to him?
--Dunno...

00:06:19.230 --> 00:06:20.970
Hello?

00:06:20.970 --> 00:06:25.170
Good to hear from you again!
Yes, we'll accept.

00:06:25.170 --> 00:06:29.180
So you want us to crush
30 street gang members, unarmed?

00:06:29.180 --> 00:06:31.450
At a suburban shopping center?

00:06:31.450 --> 00:06:35.180
OK. Our expert can
take care of them in half a day.

00:06:35.180 --> 00:06:37.090
Talk to you soon!

00:06:37.090 --> 00:06:38.990
Jo! We got a job!

00:06:42.060 --> 00:06:45.690
--Sei. Who am I after?!
--Nobody, yet.

00:06:45.690 --> 00:06:49.300
You're going to protect a
citizens' patrol tomorrow morning.

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:51.370
Rest up until then.

00:06:51.370 --> 00:06:56.300
Maybe I'll find those three
on the guest list and mess with 'em!

00:06:56.300 --> 00:07:00.540
No. You should go out
and play like a child.

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:01.880
Eh?!

00:07:01.880 --> 00:07:06.610
--Hey, Kyohei! You go play, too!
--Alright...

00:07:06.610 --> 00:07:09.140
Yahoo!

00:07:11.120 --> 00:07:12.680
Yay!

00:07:16.720 --> 00:07:18.720
--This is so fun!
--This is so fun!

00:07:25.330 --> 00:07:28.300
No one can stop me!

00:07:36.280 --> 00:07:39.780
What are you doing for
someone at your age?!

00:07:39.780 --> 00:07:42.280
Don't you have any common sense?!

00:07:42.280 --> 00:07:44.410
I'm sorry...

00:07:54.460 --> 00:07:56.600
They're really amazing...

00:07:56.600 --> 00:07:58.770
You must be exhausted.

00:07:58.770 --> 00:08:00.400
Sei-<i>san</i>...

00:08:00.400 --> 00:08:03.860
It's nice and cold. Drink up.

00:08:05.540 --> 00:08:08.210
Thank you, Sei-<i>san</i>...!

00:08:08.210 --> 00:08:12.250
Say, Kyohei-<i>kun</i>.
I have a favor to ask...

00:08:12.250 --> 00:08:15.720
My grandfather's friends are
having a dinner party tomorrow.

00:08:15.720 --> 00:08:20.560
They're really picky, so I'd
like to borrow your skills.

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:24.330
Sure, no problem! So what should I make?

00:08:24.330 --> 00:08:28.700
Enough of your special desserts
for 1000 people.

00:08:28.700 --> 00:08:30.500
One thousand...?!

00:08:30.500 --> 00:08:33.430
--Um, that's a little--
--I'm counting on you!

00:08:33.430 --> 00:08:34.840
Hold on...!

00:08:34.840 --> 00:08:38.370
Good luck, Kyohei-<i>kun</i>! You're young;
you can pull an all-nighter!

00:08:38.370 --> 00:08:40.840
I'd like some of those desserts too!

00:08:40.840 --> 00:08:44.150
Eh? They're that good?!
Then count me in, too!

00:08:44.150 --> 00:08:45.450
Good for you, Kyohei.

00:08:45.450 --> 00:08:48.720
No! There's nothing good about this!

00:08:48.720 --> 00:08:51.150
I'm sorry. I was just teasing you.

00:08:51.150 --> 00:08:54.350
Eh?! Sei-<i>san</i>...

00:08:55.190 --> 00:08:59.730
Right. That's not the motor
we're hearing; it's something else.

00:08:59.730 --> 00:09:02.360
There's no need to double-check.

00:09:02.360 --> 00:09:05.870
It's probably the machines settling in.

00:09:05.870 --> 00:09:09.200
Understood...!
I'll put it on the list.

00:09:14.640 --> 00:09:16.610
Just my imagination...

00:09:37.170 --> 00:09:41.370
--What?
--Feels nice, doesn't it?

00:09:41.370 --> 00:09:43.560
Yeah, a little.

00:09:44.510 --> 00:09:47.170
You're really odd, you know that?

00:09:48.010 --> 00:09:51.880
You haven't changed one bit
since we first met...

00:09:51.880 --> 00:09:56.380
Everything shocked me
when I came to this country.

00:09:56.380 --> 00:09:58.410
To think a day like this would come...

00:09:59.990 --> 00:10:03.580
It's like being here
and doing this isn't real...

00:10:04.860 --> 00:10:08.730
I wish every day was like this!

00:10:08.730 --> 00:10:11.270
You do?

00:10:11.270 --> 00:10:13.030
Say, Jo...

00:10:15.170 --> 00:10:23.380
I sometimes wonder what
you were like before you met me...

00:10:23.380 --> 00:10:29.320
I'm thinking you fought
against something every day...

00:10:29.320 --> 00:10:34.320
But it's like you're
always fighting something,

00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:37.660
whether you're working or not.

00:10:37.660 --> 00:10:42.360
Nothing else seems
to interest you at all...

00:10:42.360 --> 00:10:45.090
I guess that's not all bad, though!

00:11:26.070 --> 00:11:30.450
It's you I fight for, Meg.

00:11:30.450 --> 00:11:31.710
Really?

00:11:31.710 --> 00:11:35.410
Yeah. You did save me, after all.

00:11:36.250 --> 00:11:39.050
Really? You really feel that way?

00:11:41.060 --> 00:11:42.920
Yeah. Really.

00:11:43.890 --> 00:11:45.520
Jo...

00:11:48.230 --> 00:11:55.100
I'm... I'm really glad I met you, too...

00:12:07.580 --> 00:12:12.210
I did it! Wow, this really
is a huge place!

00:12:22.130 --> 00:12:24.190
Jo? What're you doing?

00:12:25.030 --> 00:12:28.560
--I can hear it...
--Hear what...?

00:12:31.710 --> 00:12:33.200
What is this?

00:12:35.880 --> 00:12:38.650
Your attention, please.

00:12:38.650 --> 00:12:43.850
We will now be re-checking all
facilities on Tokyo Treasure Island.

00:12:43.850 --> 00:12:44.750
Meg! Let's go!

00:12:44.750 --> 00:12:47.090
--What is it?
--We deeply apologize,

00:12:47.090 --> 00:12:52.160
but we ask that everyone
temporarily leave.

00:12:52.160 --> 00:12:55.900
We also ask that you do <i>not</i> smoke,

00:12:55.900 --> 00:13:00.430
in the slight chance
that something happens.

00:13:01.440 --> 00:13:03.240
No smoking?

00:13:03.240 --> 00:13:07.510
--This must be why.
--What is this? Gross!

00:13:07.510 --> 00:13:11.410
Seems a tanker got into a
mysterious collision near here...

00:13:11.410 --> 00:13:14.520
Ah, so that's why...

00:13:14.520 --> 00:13:18.920
One spark and the whole
place'll be like a frying pan.

00:13:18.920 --> 00:13:20.250
Are you serious?!

00:13:20.250 --> 00:13:24.930
Slight chance?! If they know
we're in danger, they should say so!

00:13:24.930 --> 00:13:30.360
That would only cause panic.
Let's hurry, too.

00:13:30.360 --> 00:13:34.470
--Oh, come on!
--Mommy! I wanna play more!

00:13:34.470 --> 00:13:36.200
What a disappointment.

00:13:39.710 --> 00:13:42.210
Oil fence at 60% completion.

00:13:42.210 --> 00:13:45.710
But it's flowing faster
than we can anticipate it!

00:13:45.710 --> 00:13:49.350
The shuttle bus has arrived.
Beginning evacuation.

00:13:49.350 --> 00:13:51.390
What the...?!

00:13:51.390 --> 00:13:53.820
Please board quickly and calmly!

00:13:53.820 --> 00:13:57.450
Please lead all children by the hand!

00:14:00.430 --> 00:14:02.400
--What is that?!
--An earthquake?

00:14:15.740 --> 00:14:19.950
What's the deal?! Act a
little lively, you guys!

00:14:19.950 --> 00:14:23.220
Can't when there's no one around!

00:14:23.220 --> 00:14:27.210
And I worked so hard to get tickets
through my dad's connections...

00:14:28.860 --> 00:14:31.350
Act a little grateful, will ya?!

00:14:31.860 --> 00:14:34.060
Hey, look.

00:14:34.060 --> 00:14:36.430
Huh? Is something interesting going on?

00:14:36.430 --> 00:14:37.660
Where?

00:14:52.980 --> 00:14:54.710
Oh no!

00:14:56.620 --> 00:14:58.740
--No way...!
--No way...!
--No way...!

00:15:04.230 --> 00:15:05.890
This is bad.

00:15:05.890 --> 00:15:09.500
Yes. The trailer's on the opposite shore,

00:15:09.500 --> 00:15:11.630
and we can't get over the flames...

00:15:11.630 --> 00:15:15.540
--So what's gonna happen?!
--Probably nothing.

00:15:15.540 --> 00:15:19.410
How can you all be so calm?!

00:15:19.410 --> 00:15:22.340
For now, let's get on a rooftop
and wait for help.

00:15:22.340 --> 00:15:24.540
Agreed. Let's hurry.

00:15:29.450 --> 00:15:31.150
Great! A chopper!

00:15:31.150 --> 00:15:34.020
--Leon-<i>chin</i>! Can you fly it?
--Leave it to me!

00:15:37.960 --> 00:15:39.320
What the...?!

00:15:43.100 --> 00:15:46.530
--No way...! The chopper's scrapped!
--What is that?

00:15:46.530 --> 00:15:50.200
--An octopus?
--No octopuses get that big, dummy!

00:15:50.200 --> 00:15:52.410
I think it's a squid...

00:15:52.410 --> 00:15:54.870
A monster squid, in other words...!

00:15:55.880 --> 00:15:58.650
Some people were left behind?!

00:15:58.650 --> 00:16:02.650
That's what the
shuttle bus driver reported.

00:16:02.650 --> 00:16:06.050
Any attempt to rescue them from
that sea of flames would be hopeless.

00:16:06.050 --> 00:16:11.660
Fine. The issue now is
who to blame this on.

00:16:11.660 --> 00:16:17.000
Wasn't there an environmental group
opposed to its construction?

00:16:17.000 --> 00:16:20.670
Pin this on them. Can you do that?

00:16:20.670 --> 00:16:22.070
Yes, sir.

00:16:22.070 --> 00:16:26.470
Be sure to gather evidence and
present it at the press conference.

00:16:26.470 --> 00:16:27.500
I'm counting on you.

00:16:29.880 --> 00:16:31.540
Let go!

00:16:35.680 --> 00:16:37.150
Sei-<i>san</i>!

00:16:40.450 --> 00:16:43.360
Sorry I'm so heavy...!

00:16:43.360 --> 00:16:46.260
This is one slimy situation...

00:16:46.260 --> 00:16:49.730
This is no time for puns!
What're we gonna do?!

00:16:49.730 --> 00:16:54.970
I bet the squid god got mad
because you ate too many cooked squids!

00:16:54.970 --> 00:16:57.700
Squids don't have a god!

00:17:02.110 --> 00:17:04.210
You...!

00:17:04.210 --> 00:17:06.240
Why didn't you get on the bus?!

00:17:07.620 --> 00:17:11.250
We were sneaking around...
Then my cigarette--

00:17:11.250 --> 00:17:14.760
The whole place just
burst into flames...!

00:17:14.760 --> 00:17:18.530
Ah. So <i>you</i> started the fire.

00:17:18.530 --> 00:17:21.130
This is all because you invited us!

00:17:21.130 --> 00:17:25.570
Shut up! Don't blame me!
You guys were all excited to come!

00:17:25.570 --> 00:17:28.100
What?!

00:17:28.100 --> 00:17:29.630
Shut up.

00:17:31.040 --> 00:17:33.870
We're sorry! Please forgive us!

00:17:35.380 --> 00:17:36.710
Give it over!

00:17:39.010 --> 00:17:41.080
Jo. What are you doing?

00:17:41.080 --> 00:17:44.190
Amy. Get things ready
once I'm in the air!

00:17:44.190 --> 00:17:46.150
Eh? Get what ready?

00:17:46.150 --> 00:17:49.120
The stuff so I can take
care of that monster squid!

00:17:54.830 --> 00:17:57.320
Oh, man! Jo is so cool!

00:18:01.740 --> 00:18:05.200
Jo!

00:18:07.480 --> 00:18:11.040
--Oh no! She's--
--Ah! She got sent flying on purpose!

00:18:11.880 --> 00:18:14.150
What for?!

00:18:14.150 --> 00:18:19.420
To get over the wall of flames...
Talk about reckless...

00:18:19.420 --> 00:18:22.760
Amy. Use the remote control
to open the hangar door!

00:18:22.760 --> 00:18:26.860
Ah! So that's what she meant!

00:18:26.860 --> 00:18:28.300
Jo!

00:18:28.300 --> 00:18:31.490
Seems she's the only one
who doesn't understand.

00:18:33.830 --> 00:18:37.770
The ignited crude oil has
flowed inside the building!

00:18:37.770 --> 00:18:40.940
No, I don't wanna die here!

00:18:40.940 --> 00:18:43.040
Help! Someone!

00:18:43.040 --> 00:18:46.410
Idiots! Accept your fate like men!

00:18:46.410 --> 00:18:48.470
Oh! Here she is!

00:18:51.690 --> 00:18:54.120
Jo! You're alive!

00:19:01.900 --> 00:19:03.730
You guys alright?!

00:19:28.260 --> 00:19:30.350
There's no end to this!

00:19:32.260 --> 00:19:35.490
What the...? I can't see!

00:20:17.340 --> 00:20:19.030
Smelly...!

00:20:24.550 --> 00:20:29.820
It's completely black!
And I just waxed it, too...!

00:20:29.820 --> 00:20:31.750
Couldn't be helped in this situation.

00:20:31.750 --> 00:20:34.320
What?! This is why you get on my--

00:20:34.320 --> 00:20:36.820
Now, now! All that matters
is that we're safe!

00:20:36.820 --> 00:20:41.920
--My poor Django...!
--You're all black too, you know!

00:20:47.230 --> 00:20:52.210
Fortunately, all the late
evacuees made it out safely.

00:20:52.210 --> 00:20:55.780
The cause of the accident
is under investigation,

00:20:55.780 --> 00:20:59.680
but we also have information
that an environmental group

00:20:59.680 --> 00:21:03.080
intent on preventing the
urbanization of Tokyo was involved.

00:21:03.080 --> 00:21:07.960
If true, then this was an
indiscriminate mass murder attempt.

00:21:07.960 --> 00:21:10.290
an absolutely inexcusable act.

00:21:10.290 --> 00:21:13.730
I shall make an
exhaustive examination of--

00:21:15.960 --> 00:21:19.130
I'm glad you weren't hurt,
Tachibana-<i>kun</i>!

00:21:19.130 --> 00:21:21.400
Yeah...

00:21:21.400 --> 00:21:24.800
That's what you get for
being the first ones there!

00:21:30.580 --> 00:21:31.450
"How to Make Stuffed Squid"

00:21:31.450 --> 00:21:33.080
"How to Make Stuffed Squid"
Squids!

00:21:33.080 --> 00:21:36.420
--What's wrong, Tachibana-<i>kun</i>?
--Kyohei! Pull yourself together!

00:21:36.420 --> 00:21:38.820
Squids...!

00:21:38.820 --> 00:21:40.290
Kyohei...!

00:21:56.270 --> 00:22:03.950
I remained motionless within the crowd

00:22:03.950 --> 00:22:11.590
Not even the voice of my
tears carried on this street

00:22:11.590 --> 00:22:19.300
as my feelings of lonesomeness joined it

00:22:19.300 --> 00:22:28.670
In truth, everyone wants
to smile with each other,

00:22:28.670 --> 00:22:35.210
yet they get hurt
when they can't do it very well

00:22:35.210 --> 00:22:44.220
But someone will always
be there to watch,

00:22:44.220 --> 00:22:51.020
so let's walk together
beneath this sky

00:23:12.420 --> 00:23:15.350
<i>An unknown enemy lurks in the darkness...</i>

00:23:15.350 --> 00:23:17.950
<i>A battle that's not quite
nightmare or illusion</i>

00:23:17.950 --> 00:23:20.620
<i>invites Jo into another world.</i>

00:23:20.620 --> 00:23:25.190
<i>On the next Burst Angel:</i>
"War Demon of the Haunted Realm"
